      "title": "Students",
      "description": "Employment at WKU | Western Kentucky University Your browser does not support iframes. Warning! This page requires JavaScript to be enabled in order to function properly. It appears it is currently turned off for your browser. If you need help enabling JavaScript, please contact the ITS Service Desk . Skip to main content Western Kentucky University Apply Visit More Info About WKU Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Students Campus Safety Bookstore iWKU Mobile App Dining Transportation Faculty/Staff Academic Calendar Human Resources Directory Health & Wellness myWKU Parents Family Programs Parent & Family Portal Campus Safety Cost of Attendance Member Profile Alumni Alumni Association Alumni Events Make a Gift SpiritFunder WKU SPIRIT Sign in to access Email • Blackboard • TopNet * Search WKU What majors and programs are available at WKU? How do I apply for financial aid and scholarships? Where can I register for a campus tour? What housing options are available? How can I contact an academic advisor? Sign in to access Email • Blackboard • TopNet Make a Gift Employment Work at WKU WKU Human Resources Human Resources Careers Prospective Employees Career Opportunities Equal Employment Opportunity About WKU Relocating to Bowling Green Current Employees Working at WKU Benefits Employee Wellness & Benefits Work-Life Balance Retirement Family & Medical Leave Educational Benefits Vendors' Contact Info Perks & Discounts for Employees Pay Administration Employee Tools Employee Tools New to WKU Forms Holiday Calendar EPAFs Hiring Toolkit Hiring Process Interview Exchange Resources Background Check Request Employee Development Staff Onboarding C.L.I.M.B. Higher: Equipping for Success Performance Development Reflection and Goal Setting Staff Excellence Awards Training Calendar Policies HR Policies State & Federal Notices Contact Us HR Service Tickets Staff Directory Ombuds Officer Map + Directions Why Choose WKU? Western Kentucky University (WKU) is a student-centered, applied-research institution\n                        committed to providing its students with a transformative academic and social experience\n                        and to elevating its surrounding communities.  Founded in 1906, WKU is the third largest\n                        public four-year institution in the Commonwealth of Kentucky with approximately 16,293\n                        students and nearly 2,612 faculty and staff employees*. Western Kentucky University is committed to empowering its campus community. At the\n                        heart of our mission, we seek to provide holistic education and employment experiences\n                        that prepare students, faculty, and staff to become effective scholars, contributors,\n                        and leaders in our ever-evolving communities. Located 65 miles north of Nashville, TN, and just over 100 miles south of Louisville,\n                        KY, WKU's main campus is in Bowling Green, KY - a city with approximately 70,000 residents.\n                        Our population is ethnically diverse, with more than 85 languages spoken in and around\n                        Bowling Green, and people from 35 nationalities call our community home. Western Kentucky University seeks to attract talented faculty and staff who are inspired\n                        individually to contribute to WKU's strategic plans and ongoing success. We offer\n                        comprehensive wellness and health benefits to employees and their families, including\n                        domestic partners and other qualified dependents and take pride in providing a workplace\n                        culture that supports balancing the responsibilities of work and family life. Paid-time\n                        off for holidays, vacation and sick leave, and a tuition discount program for employees\n                        and dependents are also provided. Learn more about WKU and Bowling Green at wku.edu/about . *Spring 2025 data; updated annually Returning Applicant Login Show Filters Categories Faculty Faculty (Part Time) Staff Temporary/Time Limited Clear Category Filters Locations Bowling Green, KY Elizabethtown, KY Elizabethtown/Fort Knox, KY Elizabethtown/Ft. Knox, KY Glasgow, KY Owensboro, KY Somerset, KY Clear Location Filters Sort By Date Posted (Newest) Date Posted (Oldest) Relevant Apply Filter Search Search Residence Hall Director-Campus Flats Department: Housing & Residence Life Posted On: Sep, 2nd 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Staff Show Job Details for Residence Hall Director-Campus Flats Apply Now for Residence Hall Director-Campus Flats The residence hall system has a capacity of almost 5,200 students and is comprised of 13 halls and 4 apartment buildings, offering a variety of living options: traditional, suite style living, community living, and a twelve-month extended living hall. Housing and Residence Life at WKU believes in the transformational experience that living on campus can have on a student and its integral role in the overall collegiate experience. HRL prioritizes creating a residential environment that is compatible with and supportive of the student's personal, social, and academic development. The goal of our professional staff members is to help students work towards success by developing connections with their peers, University resources, and the WKU campus community. The Residence Hall Director (RHD) is an innovative, full-time, live-on, professional staff member in a dynamic department committed to creating and sustaining supportive learning environments and helping students to reach their curricular and co-curricular goals. This integral member of the Housing and Residence Life team is responsible for the administrative and managerial functions of one or more residence halls and reports directly to an Area Coordinator. Primary Duties and Responsibilities The following duties are customary for this position but are not to be construed as all-inclusive. Duties may be added, deleted and assigned based on management discretion and institutional needs. Responsible for all general administrative and managerial functions of a residence hall(s) housing approximately 200-400 residents Responsible for the recruitment, selection, training, and supervision of 15-30 student staff members Implement student success strategies and initiatives for student success Oversee management of a 24-hour information and customer service desk(s) and its staff Facilitate programming and implement community development plan Advise, counsel, and seek to develop residents in alignment with the department's mission, vision, and goals to create and sustain a supportive living environment Serves in on-call rotation for half of campus, serving up to 2,500 students at a time Adjudicates educational disciplinary conferences for policy violations within the residence hall Creating a Supportive Learning Environment Establish rapport and develop mentoring relationships with residents to reduce barriers to success, including mental health concerns, degree or career pathway issues/decisions, and financial aid issues, making referrals when necessary Implement academic initiatives that promote student success and increase retention as part of departmental and university strategic plan Collaborate with academic and University partners to create and sustain residential communities that foster student learning, development, and academic success Plan and present residence hall and campus-wide educational and social programs Play an integral role in executing the first-year student transition program Administrative and Managerial Functions Execute administrative functions and manage daily operations of a residence hall(s) Plan and facilitate on-going training and development for student staff Report, record, and follow-up on facility, maintenance, and security issues within the hall Serve and actively contribute to the success of various departmental committees, task forces, and recruitment efforts Utilize various software solutions to manage hall occupancy, student staff scheduling, mail and package handling, conduct intervention reporting, etc. Execute crisis response protocols to maintain continuity of resident safety, security and comfort Respond to crises and other facilities, safety, and security issues in hall area via a rotating on-call schedule Collaborate with housekeeping and facilities staff members to maintain a living environment conducive to learning Essential Skills Needed Must be able to create connections with residential students to guide them to success Must possess the ability to maintain effective, cooperative working relationships with supervisors and co-workers in keeping with the values and mission of both the Department and the University Must possess above average oral, written, and computer communication skills and practice ethical decision making Must demonstrate willingness to role model acceptance and advocacy of diverse student populations by promoting a living and working environment committed to valuing diversity and social justice Must be willing to serve as a role model for residential students, student staff members, and co-workers in work ethic, attitude, and approach to work Must demonstrate an understanding of supervision of student staff members Must be willing to work evenings and high-volume weekends, and assume additional responsibilities within the department as needed Must reside in a designated professional staff apartment within the assigned residence hall for the duration of employment with Housing and Residence Life. This is a live-in position; the Residence Hall Director is required to reside in a designated professional staff apartment within the assigned residence hall for the duration of their employment with Housing and Residence Life at WKU. Although the majority of the position will function as described, some aspects are subject to change due to evolving departmental needs. Job Requirements: Bachelor's degree At least one (1) year previous experience as a Hall Director, Resident Assistant, Community Advisor, or other housing/residence life related leadership role Additional Information: Salary:  $43,896 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Academic Coordinator, TRIO Educational Talent Search Department: Educational Enhancement Programs Posted On: Sep, 1st 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Staff Show Job Details for Academic Coordinator, TRIO Educational Talent Search Apply Now for Academic Coordinator, TRIO Educational Talent Search About Educational Talent Search (ETS): Educational Talent Search at WKU is a grant-funded TRIO program funded by the Department of Education. ETS provides support, opportunities, and services to help participants succeed in their high school performance and in their higher education pursuits. ETS serves middle and high school students from low-income and first-generation households. The goal of ETS is to increase the rate participants complete high school and complete a postsecondary degree. Primary Duties and Responsibilities: The following duties are customary for this position, but are not to be construed as all-inclusive. Duties may be added, deleted, and assigned based on management discretion and institutional needs. Focus on low-income and first-generation student populations Provide pre-college awareness and services to participants and their families at target schools and in their communities Keep detailed records of services provided and participants' eligibility, including maintaining file hardware, software and paper files of participants Assist with curriculum development and activity planning Attend professional meetings and trainings, and participate in professional organizations Frequent travel to target schools and professional development conferences and/or trainings This individual will also assist the director with other duties and grant related responsibilities as necessary Knowledge and Skills Considered Essential for Success: Knowledge of educational, career and financial aid counseling. Knowledge of high school academic preparation, testing, and other issues affecting admittance to and retention in postsecondary institutions. The ability to work independently and effectively with staff, participants, parents, community partners and school personnel of diverse backgrounds and varying educational levels. Strategic planning skills and the ability to collaborate with and motivate others is critical for this position. Demonstrate effective presentation and communication skills. The ability to initiate, implement and coordinate projects. Demonstrate computer skills to effectively conduct electronically based business, communication, record keeping, presentations, and utilization of campus resources. Strong desire to promote educational achievement and opportunity. Willing to become familiar with TRIO regulations that govern program policies and procedures. Job Requirements: Bachelor's degree Minimum one year of experience in an education or community agency setting Minimum one year experience working with disadvantaged students Possess a valid driver's license with a good driving record The ability to physically lift 30 pounds The availability to work nights and weekends Additional Information: This is a grant-funded position.  Continuation is dependent upon funding/need. Salary: $36,000 - $39,000 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, should notify the office of Institutional Equity. To request an accommodation, report a complaint, or ask questions regarding WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy (#0.2040), please contact Ms. Ena Demir, Executive Director/Title IX Coordinator via email at ena.demir@wku.edu or by phone at (270) 745-6867. Ms. Demir is also responsible for coordinating the University's response to complaints related to sex and gender harassment. Additional information regarding Title IX is accessible via WKU's https://www.wku.edu/titleix/ website. Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: http://www.wku.edu/atwku/academics.php For information related to job postings, please email employment@wku.edu . Part-time Office Assistant, Theatre and Dance Box Department: Theatre & Dance Posted On: Sep, 1st 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Staff Show Job Details for Part-time Office Assistant, Theatre and Dance Box Apply Now for Part-time Office Assistant, Theatre and Dance Box Part-time Box Office Assistant to help with the day-to-day logistics of running a box office with 3 performance venues. Keeping track of performance calendar, Move and set up computers and ticket printers to appropriate venue at least one day before each production, Set up and retrieve cash boxes for each production, Printing signage and any other documents as needed, Learn ShoWare ticketing program, Help with performances as needed, Co-ordinate with Fine Arts Box Office management, Assist with other assignments as needed. Job Requirements: Qualifications for Box Office Assistant HS Diploma or GED Ability to work nights and weekends as needed. Ability to work with university students and staff. Proficient written and verbal communication skills, computer and typing skills, and demonstrated capacity for detail-oriented work are required. Applicants should exhibit organizational skills, professionalism, accountability, and initiative. Physical Abilities Required Must be able to perform physical labor, which includes climbing stairs, lifting up to 50 Ibs, carrying, reaching, standing, walking, stooping, and kneeling. Additional Information: Hourly Rate:  $16.00 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Assistant/Associate Professor - Organizational Leadership Department: School of Leadership & Professional Studies Posted On: Sep, 1st 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Faculty Show Job Details for Assistant/Associate Professor - Organizational Leadership Apply Now for Assistant/Associate Professor - Organizational Leadership Western Kentucky University is seeking to fill the position of Assistant or Associate Professor, Organizational Leadership in the School of Leadership and Professional Studies | College of Education and Behavioral Sciences This is a full-time, tenure-eligible, nine-month appointment beginning in the Fall of 2027. The Opportunity The School of Leadership and Professional Studies invites applications for a full-time, tenure-eligible faculty position in Organizational Leadership at the rank of assistant or associate professor. This is a chance to shape a growing program that prepares leaders across education, business, government, and the nonprofit sector to use data and evidence to guide decisions in their organizations. Candidates who bring both scholarly rigor and real-world leadership experience will find a program built to use both. Salary: Commensurate with rank, qualifications, and experience. What You Will Do Teaching and Advising Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in the program across multiple modalities, including online, hybrid, face-to-face, and on-demand formats Advise students and support their progress toward degree completion Teach sections of the university's learning-strategies course in support of the school's student success priorities Scholarship Conduct and publish peer-reviewed research in leadership or a closely related discipline Present at professional conferences in areas connected to the program's mission and to recruitment and retention efforts Program and Faculty Support Support curriculum assessment, development, and design Mentor and support the professional development of part-time and adjunct faculty Serve on department, college, and university committees as assigned Maintain a consistent on-campus presence, including office hours aligned with department expectations Candidates applying at the associate rank must demonstrate research and academic activity consistent with the department's promotion and tenure policy. That policy is provided to finalists at the time on-campus interviews are scheduled. About the School SLPS is a growing academic unit focused on developing adaptive leaders who can collect, analyze, and apply data to make sound decisions in their organizations. WKU is a residential campus, and faculty engage directly with students and colleagues as part of that community. Job Requirements: A PhD from a regionally accredited university in Leadership, Organizational Leadership, Leadership Studies, or a closely related field, with at least 18 hours of graduate coursework in the discipline. An EdD will be considered. Senior or executive-level leadership experience in an organizational setting. This may include higher education, business and industry, nonprofit organizations, public administration, or comparable settings. Graduate-level teaching experience (associate professor candidates). A record of, or clear capacity for, peer-reviewed publication in the discipline. Experience with curriculum assessment, development, and design. Additional Information: Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Clinical Assistant Professor, Communications Sciences and Disorders Department: Communication Sciences & Disorders Posted On: Sep, 1st 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Faculty Show Job Details for Clinical Assistant Professor, Communications Sciences and Disorders Apply Now for Clinical Assistant Professor, Communications Sciences and Disorders The Communications Sciences and Disorders Department seeking candidates for a full-time (9-month) non-tenure-track appointment of Clinical Assistant Professor effective January 2027. The Communications Sciences and Disorders Department is housed within the College of Health and Human Services and offers undergraduate programs in Communication Sciences & Disorders. The Department also offers graduate programs in Speech Language Pathology. Please see the website for more information on our programs: http://www.wku.edu/communicationdisorders/. The following duties are customary for this position, but are not to be construed as all-inclusive.  Duties may be added, deleted, and assigned based on management discretion as well as departmental and institutional needs. Expectations will be weighed differently depending on the strengths of the candidate and the needs of the department. Clinical supervision of undergraduate and graduate students Undergraduate student advising as needed Instruction at the undergraduate level Possible instruction of elective graduate courses in an area of expertise Service to the department, college, university, and/or profession All successful candidates must have the ability to engage in alternative modes of instructional delivery which may include synchronous online (distance learning) courses, and/or IVS.  Instruction modality is based on assigned teaching duties. Job Requirements: Master's degree in Speech and Language Pathology Certificate of Clinical Competence (CCC) in Speech and Language Pathology Holds or is eligible for KY licensure in area of clinical certification At least three years of post-masters experience At least two years of clinical supervisory experience Strong communication skills Evidence of knowledge of technology required for assigned duties. Attention to detail and ability to work well with all levels of faculty, staff, and students Additional Information: Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Chair, Department of Mathematics Department: Mathematics Posted On: Aug, 31st 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Faculty Show Job Details for Chair, Department of Mathematics Apply Now for Chair, Department of Mathematics The Department of Mathematics at Western Kentucky University is seeking qualified applicants for the position of Department Chair. The Department is housed in the Ogden College of Science and Engineering, and has 25 full-time faculty representing a variety of backgrounds and major research areas in mathematics. The Department offers a variety of both undergraduate and graduate degrees. The Department also provides general education mathematics courses to WKU students. The Department Chair is expected to manage department operations (including the departmental budget), facilitate the direction of undergraduate and graduate programs, uphold and enhance the excellence of the department, and represent the department within the college, across the university, and in the community. Knowledge and Skills Considered Essential for Success: Administration and leadership skills, including budget management, personnel evaluation, and problem resolution. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Ability to lead faculty who specialize in pure or applied mathematics, statistics, and/or mathematics education. Ability to effectively negotiate with administration and other academic units. Ability to work effectively in a multi-ethnic/multicultural environment. Demonstrated ability to build trust through collaborative decision making. An in-depth understanding of current trends in mathematics research, teaching pedagogy, and best practices. Demonstrated ability to ensure a culture of accountability in which departmental goals and expectations are specified, and strategies are articulated. Demonstrated ability to support faculty in applying for, obtaining, and administering external funding. Job Requirements: Earned doctorate in Mathematics, Statistics, Mathematics Education, Statistics Education, or a closely related field. Ability to meet departmental standards for tenure and hold the rank of Associate or full Professor at the time of hire. Demonstrated record of excellence in teaching, research, and service. Additional Information: Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Assistant/Associate Professor, School of Leadership & Professional Studies Department: School of Leadership & Professional Studies Posted On: Aug, 28th 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Faculty Show Job Details for Assistant/Associate Professor, School of Leadership & Professional Studies Apply Now for Assistant/Associate Professor, School of Leadership & Professional Studies Assistant or Associate Professor, Educational Administration School of Leadership and Professional Studies | College of Education and Behavioral Sciences Western Kentucky University | Full-time, tenure-eligible, nine-month appointment The Opportunity The School of Leadership and Professional Studies invites applications for a full-time, tenure-eligible faculty position in Educational  Leadership and Administration at the rank of assistant or associate professor. WKU's Educational Administration program prepares school administrators across Kentucky and was one of seven university programs nationally selected for the Wallace Foundation's University Principal Preparation Initiative, a $6 million redesign undertaken in direct partnership with school districts and state agencies and centered on equity in context, and a $1.3 million dollar Department of Labor grant to create a principal apprenticeship pathway, the first of it's kind in the Commonwealth of Kentucky. The successful candidate joins a program with a demonstrated record of translating research and district partnership into practice and will teach and conduct research across a program that spans four distinct pathways for developing educational leaders. What You Will Do Teaching Teach courses in educational administration across all program pathways: MAE, Rank I, Certification Only, and EdD Scholarship Conduct and publish research in educational administration and leadership in the P-12 setting Advance a research agenda that supports the program's mission and its work on equity-centered leadership preparation Program Support Support the program's work in developing school leaders who understand the role of equity, diversity, and inclusion in education Demonstrate practice that embraces supporting the success of students from diverse backgrounds through teaching, advising, and research *Candidates applying at the associate rank must demonstrate research and academic activity consistent with the department's promotion and tenure policy. That policy is provided to finalists at the time on-campus interviews are scheduled. Job Requirements: The successful candidate will bring: An EdD or PhD in Educational Leadership, Educational Administration, or a closely related field from an accredited university At least three years of experience as a school principal, or a combined five years of experience as a principal and central office administrator A demonstrated ability to advance a research agenda in educational leadership that supports the program's mission (*associate professor candidates) Experience supporting the success of students from diverse backgrounds in educational leadership Additional Information: Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Director, Educational Talent Search Department: Educational Enhancement Programs Posted On: Aug, 28th 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Staff Show Job Details for Director, Educational Talent Search Apply Now for Director, Educational Talent Search The Director oversees all aspects of the federally-funded Talent Search (TS) program (as outlined in the grant), including staff supervision and management, and the development of programs focused on middle school/high school student success, graduation, and postsecondary enrollment.  The Director works with key internal and external stakeholders to implement programs that support the success of TS-eligible populations, including student populations from lower socio-economic backgrounds. This is a grant-funded position. Continuation is dependent upon funding/need. Administration & Personnel Supervise, hire, train, and evaluate program staff Manage daily operations across all target schools Develop and administer the annual program budget Maintain student records and data systems Program & Direct Services Provide academic, career, and financial aid advising Coordinate college visits and application assistance Lead FAFSA workshops and financial literacy activities Organize tutoring, test prep, and student programming Compliance & Reporting Ensure compliance with TRIO and federal grant regulations Prepare and submit the Annual Performance Report (APR) Verify participant eligibility and required documentation Maintain audit-ready files for program reviews Partnerships & Community Relations Build relationships with partner school staff and counselors Represent the program with colleges and community organizations Serve as liaison to WKU leadership and TRIO stakeholders Job Requirements: Master's degree from an accredited institution (field such as education, counseling, higher education administration, social work, or related field) Valid driver's license and ability to travel to target schools; ability to work some evenings/weekends Ability to lift 25 lbs. Additional Information: Salary Range:  $58,000 - $60,000 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Specialist, Graduate Student Advising and Retention, Teacher Education Department: School of Teacher Education Posted On: Aug, 26th 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Staff Show Job Details for Specialist, Graduate Student Advising and Retention, Teacher Education Apply Now for Specialist, Graduate Student Advising and Retention, Teacher Education The School of Teacher Education (STE) within the College of Education and Behavioral Sciences is seeking applications for the position of Specialist for Graduate Student Advising and Retention. The Specialist is responsible for supporting graduate students and the graduate programs within STE. This position reports to the Director of the School of Teacher Education. Duties include: Student Services and Support Serve as the first point of contact for prospective and current graduate students Advise prospective students through the admissions process, answering questions about program requirements, certification options, and application procedures Monitor student progress and communicate with at risk students to provide support and resources Address student concerns and questions regarding WKU and Graduate School policies, procedures, registration, and academic requirements Maintain regular communication with online students to foster engagement and connection to the college Collaborate with the Graduate School and Office of Professional Educator Services to create a streamlined pathway to graduation and teacher certification Recruitment and Marketing Services Assist with recruitment initiatives and marketing efforts for graduate programs in the School of Teacher Education Represent the programs at virtual recruitment events, information sessions, and webinars Coordinate with the admissions office to analyze enrollment trends, track application pipelines, and follow up with prospective students Program Administration Assist with graduate processes and new initiatives within the School of Teacher Education Maintain graduate records Support alternate certification options including CEO and Proficiency candidates Support the STE Director and Assistant Director as needed for graduate programming Other duties as assigned Working Conditions: This is NOT a remote position Standard working hours from 8:00-4:30pm Occasional evening or weekend hours may be required for events or student support May require periodic travel for conferences or recruitment events Knowledge and Skills Considered Essential for Success Excellent interpersonal and communication skills (written and verbal) Strong customer service orientation Microsoft Office Suite Exceptional organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment Commitment to maintaining confidentiality and adhering to FERPA regulations Job Requirements: Master's Degree Additional Information: Salary: $45,000 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Assistant, Associate, or Full (Open Rank) Professor, Clinical PSY Department: Psychology Posted On: Aug, 26th 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Faculty Show Job Details for Assistant, Associate, or Full (Open Rank) Professor, Clinical PSY Apply Now for Assistant, Associate, or Full (Open Rank) Professor, Clinical PSY Western Kentucky University's Psychology Department (www.wku.edu/psychology/) is seeking qualified applicants for a full-time, 9-month, tenure-eligible Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor position in clinical psychology beginning August 2027. This position will primarily support the clinical psychology master's program, but the Department of Psychology also has an undergraduate major in psychology, an APA-Accredited PsyD in clinical psychology, and an education specialist program in school psychology. The Department of Psychology is housed in the collaborative College of Education and Behavioral Sciences, which also has programs in teacher education, counseling, educational leadership and administration, military sciences, and more. Responsibilities for the position include teaching graduate (e.g., intellectual assessment, psychopathology, psychotherapy practicum) and undergraduate coursework (e.g., abnormal psychology, behavior modification); conducting scholarly research and publishing; advising graduate and undergraduate students; and guiding graduate research as well as serving on graduate research committees (i.e., thesis and dissertation committees). Additional responsibilities include serving on program, department, college, or university committees, and other duties as assigned. WKU's Department of Psychology is committed to initiatives pertaining to first generation students and promoting inclusive excellence overall, while increasing the diversity of the University community. Candidates who can contribute to that goal are encouraged to apply and to identify their strengths or experiences in this area. Job Requirements: All applicants must have an earned doctorate in clinical psychology or a related field by the posted start date. Candidates should be licensed or license eligible as a Licensed Psychologist in the Commonwealth of Kentucky. Additional requirements for each rank are below. Assistant Professor: Candidate is expected to demonstrate potential for excellence in teaching and have an active and productive program of scholarly research. Associate Professor: Candidate must have 6+ years experience in higher education, demonstrate excellence in teaching graduate and undergraduate courses, evidence of sustained scholarly activity including publications and presentations, and a record of service to the institution and profession. Full Professor: Candidate must have earned tenure at another institution, have 12+ years experience in higher education, demonstrate excellence in teaching graduate and undergraduate courses, evidence of sustained scholarly activity including publications and presentations, and a record of service to the institution and profession. Additional Information: Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . First Previous 1 (current) 2 3 4 5 Next Last Some of the links on this page may require additional software to view. Downloads Download Acrobat Reader Download Quicktime Western Kentucky University 1906 College Heights Blvd. Bowling Green, KY 42101 Search WKU About WKU Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Transparency & Accountability Accessibility Title IX Careers Statement of Non-Discrimination Contact Us Site Index Privacy Statement Last Modified 9/17/25"
    },
    "https://www.wku.edu/hr/careers/newtowku.php": {
      "title": "Welcome to WKU! Starting a new position can be both exciting and overwhelming.  Here",
      "description": "New to WKU | Western Kentucky University Your browser does not support iframes. Warning! This page requires JavaScript to be enabled in order to function properly. It appears it is currently turned off for your browser. If you need help enabling JavaScript, please contact the ITS Service Desk . Skip to main content Western Kentucky University Apply Visit More Info About WKU Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Students Campus Safety Bookstore iWKU Mobile App Dining Transportation Faculty/Staff Academic Calendar Human Resources Directory Health & Wellness myWKU Parents Family Programs Parent & Family Portal Campus Safety Cost of Attendance Member Profile Alumni Alumni Association Alumni Events Make a Gift SpiritFunder WKU SPIRIT Sign in to access Email • Blackboard • TopNet * Search WKU What majors and programs are available at WKU? How do I apply for financial aid and scholarships? Where can I register for a campus tour? What housing options are available? How can I contact an academic advisor? Sign in to access Email • Blackboard • TopNet Make a Gift New to WKU Questions? Ask HR WKU Human Resources Human Resources Careers Prospective Employees Career Opportunities Equal Employment Opportunity About WKU Relocating to Bowling Green Current Employees Working at WKU Benefits Employee Wellness & Benefits Work-Life Balance Retirement Family & Medical Leave Educational Benefits Vendors' Contact Info Perks & Discounts for Employees Pay Administration Employee Tools Employee Tools New to WKU Forms Holiday Calendar EPAFs Hiring Toolkit Hiring Process Interview Exchange Resources Background Check Request Employee Development Staff Onboarding C.L.I.M.B. Higher: Equipping for Success Performance Development Reflection and Goal Setting Staff Excellence Awards Training Calendar Policies HR Policies State & Federal Notices Contact Us HR Service Tickets Staff Directory Ombuds Officer Map + Directions Information for New Employees Welcome to WKU! Starting a new position can be both exciting and overwhelming.  Here\n                     at WKU, we wish to make your transition as smooth as possible.  Below are some important\n                     steps to help new employees get started.  Click the link based on your new position\n                     status or if you're a supervisor of a new staff employee, click on the corresponding\n                     Supervisor button. Click for Staff Click for Faculty Part-Time Employees Graduate Assistants Student Employees Staff Onboarding Human Resources Policies State & Federal Notices Full-Time Staff Full-time Staff Before You Arrive Employment Eligibility Verification All new employees will receive an email from noreply@sterling.app in order to complete a criminal background check. Once completed, new employees will\n                                    also receive an email to complete Section 1 of the Form I-9 for employment eligibility\n                                    verification. Both the I-9 and criminal background check must be successfully completed\n                                    before a new hire can begin employment at WKU. Relocating to Bowling Green? Make sure to visit our About Bowling Green page to find information that can assist with your transition to the area.  Welcome\n                                    to Bowling Green! Day 1 HR Registration All new employees must visit the WKU Department of Human Resources to complete tax\n                                    forms, direct deposit information and Section 2 of Form I9.  A list of the proper\n                                    identification you will need to bring with you to Human Resources can be found HERE . WKU Employee I.D. New employees may obtain a WKU Employee Identification Card by visiting the WKU I.D.\n                                    Center located in Downing Student Union room 2125.  Your Offer of Employment Letter and a valid photo ID will be required.  Additional information may be viewed\n                                    on the I.D. Center webpage. Access Control Have a need for building keys or other access control privileges?  Have your College/Department\n                                    hiring authority make these requests directly to WKU Access Control.  For additional\n                                    information on key pick up, customer service hours can be found HERE . Campus Parking & Transportation Parking Permits are required for all categories of long-term parking throughout campus. \n                                    The Parking and Transportation Department is located at 578 Campbell Ln.  Campus maps\n                                    and parking information can be viewed at Parking and Transportation Services . Be Prepared Knowing what to do in an emergency saves lives!  The safety and well-being of our\n                                    employees, students and visitors are our FIRST priorities!  Please review the Faculty/Staff\n                                    Emergency Procedures and sign up for Emergency Notification Text Alerts to receive accurate emergency and weather related campus notifications both of which\n                                    may be found on the WKU Police webpage.  Be certain to familiarize yourself with your building's Emergency Action Plan which may be viewed on the WKU Environmental Health & Safety webpage. Find Your Way Getting familiar with campus can be intimidating!  Find your way around campus easier\n                                    with WKU's Virtual Tour , WKU Facilities Maps , OR by using the Maps app within your iWKU app . Your First 30 Days Payroll There are multiple payroll frequencies at WKU and it's helpful to know your payroll schedule .  Your supervisor can inform you of your payroll frequency and information about\n                                    that schedule can be found on the Payroll Department's website .  A copy of the payroll handbook can be found here as well.  Your pay stubs are available in TopNet under Employee Services, you should review this each pay cycle.  Did you know you\n                                    can receive your W-2 electronically?  Log in to TopNet to opt-in to electronic receipt, found under Employee Services. Timekeeping All non-exempt employees are required to maintain an accurate record of time worked. \n                                       As required by the Fair Labor Standards Act, any hours worked over 40 during a given\n                                       workweek are to be paid at time and one half.  More information can be found by visiting\n                                       the Timekeeping section of our website. Review Your Benefit Enrollment Review and make decisions about participation in WKU’s various benefit programs. You\n                                    must enroll within the 31 days of your benefits effective date for coverage such as\n                                    Medical, Dental, Vision, etc., otherwise, you will be required to wait until the next\n                                    annual Open Enrollment period, unless you have a qualifying life event.  For those\n                                    who are TRS eligible employees, you have 30 days from your hire date to make retirement\n                                    elections. Say Cheese! Newly hired employees are encouraged to schedule an appointment with University Photography located on the 3rd floor of the Wetherby Administration Building, to have a photo\n                                    made that will be posted on the department webpage. Information Technology Services (ITS) Orientation Enroll in the ITS: New Employee Orientation course in Blackboard today!  Additionally, both full-time and part-time employees can follow\n                                    this WKU ITS New Hire Guide to get set up on all systems WKU, check out services provided by ITS. It is especially\n                                    important you complete the NetID Look-up.  Your NetID is your username for the majority\n                                    of your WKU sign-ins. Title IX Training All employees and new hires are encouraged to complete Title IX Training within the\n                                    first 30 days of employment. Title IX Training is available online at www.wku.edu/titleix along with instructions for accessing the Title IX Training(s). Be Your Best At WKU we value diversification and the extraordinary talent and experience each individual\n                                    brings to the University.  Anyone needing special accommodations to assist in performing\n                                    his or her job duties is encouraged to contact the Office of Equal Employment Opportunity to discuss WKU's ADA Policies and Procedures. Be in the Know All University policies may be viewed at the WKU University Policies webpage.  The WKU Faculty Handbook may be viewed on the Academic Affairs webpage.  Additionally, WKU has a Communication & Branding Manual that provides guidelines, templates and information to assist in ensuring the WKU\n                                    image is wholly representative of our values!  Additional information may be viewed\n                                    on the Public Affairs webpage. ... And Beyond Stay Connected Annual training, informational sessions and special events are communicated through\n                                    University e-mail, and may be viewed on the WKU Events Calendar .  All WKU employees are asked to carefully review all electronic transmissions and\n                                    respond accordingly. Also be sure to download the iWKU app , available on the App Store for iOS devices.  Although originally designed for current\n                                    WKU students, Faculty & Staff can get instant access to campus maps, building information,\n                                    operating hours, emergency alerts, news, events and more! Time away from your desk! When it comes to time away from the office, WKU is looking out for you!  WKU’s PTO\n                                    program provides employees the ability to cover any situation that may be encountered,\n                                    in addition to offering a generous holiday schedule.  A complete guide to all Work\n                                    Life Balance options WKU provides can be found on our benefits page. Get to Know Your New Home Away from Home Here at WKU there are many opportunities for staff, faculty and student growth, enrichment\n                                    and engagement.  Following are a few to help you get the most out of your WKU! WKU Preston Center - The Department of Campus Recreation & Wellness offers a variety of fun and fitness\n                                          activities for the entire family including a state-of-the-art exercise facility with\n                                          personal trainers.  Full-time employees have the option for payroll deducted membership\n                                          fee WKU Dining - The Dining and Restaurant Group offers a variety of cuisine options and meal plans\n                                          to enhance your campus dining experience.  Full-time employees receive one complimentary\n                                          meal per month at Fresh Food, compliments of Aramark. The WKU Store - Your official source for all things WKU!  All WKU employees receive a 10% discount\n                                          on WKU clothing, merchandise and memorabilia.  The store also has a technology department\n                                          featuring Apple, Dell and other brands of PCs, laptops and accessories available at\n                                          educational pricing. Downing Student Union - The Downing Student Union is the hub of student activities and engagement.  It\n                                          also houses The WKU Store the official sponsor of \" Big Red Mania!\" GO TO PS! - Hilltopper madness is everywhere!  Employees are eligible to receive discounted\n                                          tickets to Football, Men's Basketball, and Women's Basketball games. Contact 270-745-5222\n                                          for details on ticket discounts and visit WKU Sports webpage for game schedules and other Hilltopper Athletic news and events. Spirit Day is officially every Friday when students, faculty and staff are encouraged\n                                          to flaunt their WKU threads! Experience the Global Community! - The campus offers a variety of opportunities for personal growth, development,\n                                          and just plain fun!  Check out the: Cultural Enhancement Series , Concert Series , Theatre and Dance Performances , Hardin Planetarium , and L.D. Brown Ag/Expo Center to name a few! Additional WKU Perks & Discounts for Employees - It pays to be a part of the WKU Community! Enjoy special discounts and perks only\n                                          available to our employees. Discounts include local attractions, restaurants, travel,\n                                          and more! Full-Time Faculty Full-Time Faculty Human Resources Orientation Employment Eligibility Verification All new employees will receive an email from noreply@sterling.app in order to complete a criminal background check. Once completed, new employees will\n                                    also receive an email to complete Section 1 of the Form I-9 for employment eligibility\n                                    verification. Both the I-9 and criminal background check must be successfully completed\n                                    before a new hire can begin employment at WKU. Payroll There are multiple payroll frequencies at WKU and it's helpful to know your payroll schedule .  As full-time faculty, you will be paid on the Monthly payroll schedule which pays\n                                    on the last working day of each month.  The schedule can be found on the Payroll Department's website .  A copy of the payroll handbook can be found here as well.  Your pay stubs are available in TopNet under Employee Services, you should review this each pay cycle.  Did you know you\n                                    can receive your W-2 electronically?  Log in to TopNet to opt-in to electronic receipt, found under Employee Services. Review Your Benefit Enrollment Review and make decisions about participation in WKU’s various benefit programs. You\n                                    must enroll within the 31 days of your benefits effective date for coverage such as\n                                    Medical, Dental, Vision, etc., otherwise, you will be required to wait until the next\n                                    annual Open Enrollment period, unless you have a qualifying life event.  Retirement\n                                    is mandatory though you have two options- TRS or ORP.  You'll have 30 days from your\n                                    hire date to make this decision. New Faculty Guide Click here to visit the full New Faculty Checklist along with a schedule of new faculty events and other helpful resources. Part-Time Employees Part-time Employees Part-time employees and/or occasional employees are generally not eligible for benefit\n                           program participation, and therefore do not participate in New Hire Orientation, but\n                           must complete all applicable payroll tax withholding, biographical data and I-9 Employment\n                           Eligibility Forms.  The forms may be obtained from the hiring College/Department or\n                           by visiting the WKU Department of Human Resources located in the Wetherby Administration\n                           Building Rm G-25.  Please see the link for I-9 Form in Step 1 above for a list of\n                           the proper identification you will need to bring with you. Before You Arrive Employment Eligibility Verification All new employees will receive an email from noreply@sterling.app in order to complete a criminal background check. Once completed, new employees will\n                                    also receive an email to complete Section 1 of the Form I-9 for employment eligibility\n                                    verification. Both the I-9 and criminal background check must be successfully completed\n                                    before a new hire can begin employment at WKU. Day 1 HR Registration All new employees must visit the WKU Department of Human Resources to complete tax\n                                    forms, direct deposit information and Section 2 of Form I9.  A list of the proper\n                                    identification you will need to bring with you to Human Resources can be found HERE . WKU Employee I.D. New employees may obtain a WKU Employee Identification Card by visiting the WKU I.D.\n                                    Center located in Downing Student Union room 2125.  Your Offer of Employment Letter and a valid photo ID will be required.  Additional information may be viewed\n                                    on the I.D. Center webpage. Email Account Request Once your part-time staff employment status is considered active, you may request\n                                    an email account creation by submitting an online request HERE . Part-time faculty receive an email account automatically and do not need to submit\n                                    a request. Access Control Have a need for building keys or other access control privileges?  Have your College/Department\n                                    hiring authority make these requests directly to WKU Access Control.  For additional\n                                    information on key pick up, customer service hours can be found HERE . Campus Parking & Transportation Parking Permits are required for all categories of long-term parking throughout campus. \n                                    The Parking and Transportation Department is located at 578 Campbell Ln.  Campus maps\n                                    and parking information can be viewed at Parking and Transportation Services . Be Prepared Knowing what to do in an emergency saves lives!  The safety and well-being of our\n                                    employees, students and visitors are our FIRST priorities!  Please review the Faculty/Staff\n                                    Emergency Procedures and sign up for Emergency Notification Text Alerts to receive accurate emergency and weather related campus notifications both of which\n                                    may be found on the WKU Police webpage.  Be certain to familiarize yourself with your building's Emergency Action Plan which may be viewed on the WKU Environmental Health & Safety webpage. Find Your Way Getting familiar with campus can be intimidating!  Find your way around campus easier\n                                    with WKU's Virtual Tour , WKU Facilities Maps , OR by using the Maps app within your iWKU app . Your First 30 Days Payroll There are multiple payroll frequencies at WKU and it's helpful to know your payroll schedule .  Your supervisor can inform you of your payroll frequency and information about\n                                    that schedule can be found on the Payroll Department's website .  A copy of the payroll handbook can be found here as well.  Your pay stubs are available in TopNet under Employee Services, you should review this each pay cycle.  Did you know you\n                                    can receive your W-2 electronically?  Log in to TopNet to opt-in to electronic receipt, found under Employee Services. Timekeeping All non-exempt employees are required to maintain an accurate record of time worked. \n                                    As required by the Fair Labor Standards Act, any hours worked over 40 during a given\n                                    workweek are to be paid at time and one half.  More information can be found by visiting\n                                    the Timekeeping section of our website. Information Technology Services (ITS) Orientation Enroll in the ITS: New Employee Orientation course in Blackboard today! Additionally, both full-time and part-time employees can follow\n                                    this WKU ITS New Hire Guide to get set up on all systems WKU, check out services provided by ITS. It is especially\n                                    important you complete the NetID Look-up.  Your NetID is your username for the majority\n                                    of your WKU sign-ins. Title IX Training All employees and new hires are encouraged to complete Title IX Training within the\n                                    first 30 days of employment. Title IX Training is available online at www.wku.edu/titleix along with instructions for accessing the Title IX Training(s) . Be Your Best At WKU we value diversification and the extraordinary talent and experience each individual\n                                    brings to the University.  Anyone needing special accommodations to assist in performing\n                                    his or her job duties is encouraged to contact the Office of Equal Employment Opportunity to discuss WKU's ADA Policies and Procedures. Be in the Know All University policies may be viewed at the WKU University Policies webpage.  The WKU Faculty Handbook may be viewed on the Academic Affairs webpage.  Additionally, WKU has a Communication & Branding Manual that provides guidelines, templates and information to assist in ensuring the WKU\n                                    image is wholly representative of our values!  Additional information may be viewed\n                                    on the Public Affairs webpage. ... And Beyond Stay Connected Annual training, informational sessions and special events are communicated through\n                                    University e-mail, and may be viewed on the WKU Events Calendar .  All WKU employees are asked to carefully review all electronic transmissions and\n                                    respond accordingly. Also be sure to download the iWKU app , available on the App Store for iOS devices.  Although originally designed for current\n                                    WKU students, Faculty & Staff can get instant access to campus maps, building information,\n                                    operating hours, emergency alerts, news, events and more! Get to Know Your New Home Away from Home Here at WKU there are many opportunities for staff, faculty and student growth, enrichment\n                                    and engagement.  Following are a few to help you get the most out of your WKU! Get to Know Your New Home Away from Home Here at WKU there are many opportunities for staff, faculty and student growth, enrichment\n                                    and engagement.  Following are a few to help you get the most out of your WKU! WKU Preston Center - The Department of Campus Recreation & Wellness offers a variety of fun and fitness\n                                          activities for the entire family including a state-of-the-art exercise facility with\n                                          personal trainers.  Full-time employees have the option for payroll deducted membership\n                                          fee WKU Dining - The Dining and Restaurant Group offers a variety of cuisine options and meal plans\n                                          to enhance your campus dining experience.  Full-time employees receive one complimentary\n                                          meal per month at Fresh Food, compliments of Aramark. The WKU Store - Your official source for all things WKU!  All WKU employees receive a 10% discount\n                                          on WKU clothing, merchandise and memorabilia.  The store also has a technology department\n                                          featuring Apple, Dell and other brands of PCs, laptops and accessories available at\n                                          educational pricing. Downing Student Union - The Downing Student Union is the hub of student activities and engagement.  It\n                                          also houses The WKU Store the official sponsor of \" Big Red Mania!\" GO TO PS! - Hilltopper madness is everywhere!  Employees are eligible to receive discounted\n                                          tickets to Football, Men's Basketball, and Women's Basketball games. Contact 270-745-5222\n                                          for details on ticket discounts and visit WKU Sports webpage for game schedules and other Hilltopper Athletic news and events. Spirit Day is officially every Friday when students, faculty and staff are encouraged\n                                          to flaunt their WKU threads! Experience the Global Community! - The campus offers a variety of opportunities for personal growth, development,\n                                          and just plain fun!  Check out the: Cultural Enhancement Series , Concert Series , Theatre and Dance Performances , Hardin Planetarium , and L.D. Brown Ag/Expo Center to name a few! Additional WKU Perks & Discounts for Employees - It pays to be a part of the WKU Community! Enjoy special discounts and perks only\n                                          available to our employees. Discounts include local attractions, restaurants, travel,\n                                          and more! Graduate Assistants Graduate Assistants For more information on Graduate Assistantships, please visit The Graduate School. Before You Arrive Employment Eligibility Verification All new employees, including Graduate Assistants, will receive an email from noreply@sterling.app in order to complete a criminal background check. Once completed, new employees will\n                                    also receive an email to complete Section 1 of the Form I-9 for employment eligibility\n                                    verification. Day 1 HR Registration All new Graduate Assistants must visit the WKU Department of Human Resources to complete\n                                    tax forms, direct deposit information and Section 2 of Form I9 no later than three\n                                    days from the date of hire.  A list of the proper identification you will need to\n                                    bring with you to Human Resources can be found HERE . Both the I-9 (Section 1 and Section 2) and criminal background check must be successfully\n                                       completed before a new hire can begin employment at WKU. Representatives from HR will also be available during Graduate Student Orientation,\n                                    where you can complete these items. Student Employees Students Student Employment at WKU Visit the WKU Student Employment webpage .  Here you can find tax forms, information on eligibility, job vacancies and answers\n                        to Frequently Asked Questions . Employment Eligibility Verification & Student Employment Registration All new student employees will receive an email from noreply@sterling.app in order to complete a criminal background check.  Once completed, new student employees\n                        will also receive an email to complete Section 1 of the Form I-9 for employment eligibility\n                        verification. All new student employees must visit the Student Employment Office, 324 Potter Hall,\n                        to complete tax forms , and section 2 of Form I-9.  A list of the proper identification you will need to\n                        bring with you to  Student Employment can be found HERE . Both the I-9 and criminal background check must be successfully completed before\n                           you can begin employment at WKU. Some of the links on this page may require additional software to view. Downloads Download Acrobat Reader Download Quicktime Western Kentucky University 1906 College Heights Blvd. Bowling Green, KY 42101 Search WKU About WKU Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Transparency & Accountability Accessibility Title IX Careers Statement of Non-Discrimination Contact Us Site Index Privacy Statement Last Modified 4/15/26"
    },
    "http://wku.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204366": {
      "title": "Western Kentucky University \n\tJob Posting: Residence Hall Director-Campus Flats",
      "description": "Western Kentucky University\nJob Posting: Residence Hall Director-Campus Flats Western Kentucky University \n\tJob Posting: Residence Hall Director-Campus Flats Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Residence Hall Director-Campus Flats Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Housing & Residence Life Locations: Bowling Green, KY Posted: Sep 2, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 998840 Position ID: 204366 Share About Western Kentucky University: Western Kentucky University (WKU) is a student-centered, applied-research institution committed to providing its students with a transformative academic and social experience and to elevating its surrounding communities. Founded in 1906, WKU is the third largest public four-year institution in the Commonwealth of Kentucky with approximately 16,293 students and nearly 2,612 faculty and staff employees. Western Kentucky University is committed to empowering its campus community. At the heart of our mission, we seek to provide holistic education and employment experiences that prepare students, faculty, and staff to become effective scholars, contributors, and leaders in our ever-evolving communities. Located 65 miles north of Nashville, TN, and just over 100 miles south of Louisville, KY, WKU's main campus is in Bowling Green, KY - a city with approximately 70,000 residents. Our population is ethnically diverse, with more than 85 languages spoken in and around Bowling Green, and people from 35 nationalities call our community home. Western Kentucky University seeks to attract talented faculty and staff who are inspired individually to contribute to WKU's strategic plans and ongoing success. We offer comprehensive wellness and health benefits to employees and their families, including domestic partners and other qualified dependents and take pride in providing a workplace culture that supports balancing the responsibilities of work and family life. Paid-time off for holidays, vacation and sick leave, and a tuition discount program for employees and dependents are also provided. Learn more about WKU and Bowling Green at wku.edu/about . Job Description: The residence hall system has a capacity of almost 5,200 students and is comprised of 13 halls and 4 apartment buildings, offering a variety of living options: traditional, suite style living, community living, and a twelve-month extended living hall. Housing and Residence Life at WKU believes in the transformational experience that living on campus can have on a student and its integral role in the overall collegiate experience. HRL prioritizes creating a residential environment that is compatible with and supportive of the student's personal, social, and academic development. The goal of our professional staff members is to help students work towards success by developing connections with their peers, University resources, and the WKU campus community. The Residence Hall Director (RHD) is an innovative, full-time, live-on, professional staff member in a dynamic department committed to creating and sustaining supportive learning environments and helping students to reach their curricular and co-curricular goals. This integral member of the Housing and Residence Life team is responsible for the administrative and managerial functions of one or more residence halls and reports directly to an Area Coordinator. Primary Duties and Responsibilities The following duties are customary for this position but are not to be construed as all-inclusive. Duties may be added, deleted and assigned based on management discretion and institutional needs. Responsible for all general administrative and managerial functions of a residence hall(s) housing approximately 200-400 residents Responsible for the recruitment, selection, training, and supervision of 15-30 student staff members Implement student success strategies and initiatives for student success Oversee management of a 24-hour information and customer service desk(s) and its staff Facilitate programming and implement community development plan Advise, counsel, and seek to develop residents in alignment with the department's mission, vision, and goals to create and sustain a supportive living environment Serves in on-call rotation for half of campus, serving up to 2,500 students at a time Adjudicates educational disciplinary conferences for policy violations within the residence hall Creating a Supportive Learning Environment Establish rapport and develop mentoring relationships with residents to reduce barriers to success, including mental health concerns, degree or career pathway issues/decisions, and financial aid issues, making referrals when necessary Implement academic initiatives that promote student success and increase retention as part of departmental and university strategic plan Collaborate with academic and University partners to create and sustain residential communities that foster student learning, development, and academic success Plan and present residence hall and campus-wide educational and social programs Play an integral role in executing the first-year student transition program Administrative and Managerial Functions Execute administrative functions and manage daily operations of a residence hall(s) Plan and facilitate on-going training and development for student staff Report, record, and follow-up on facility, maintenance, and security issues within the hall Serve and actively contribute to the success of various departmental committees, task forces, and recruitment efforts Utilize various software solutions to manage hall occupancy, student staff scheduling, mail and package handling, conduct intervention reporting, etc. Execute crisis response protocols to maintain continuity of resident safety, security and comfort Respond to crises and other facilities, safety, and security issues in hall area via a rotating on-call schedule Collaborate with housekeeping and facilities staff members to maintain a living environment conducive to learning Essential Skills Needed Must be able to create connections with residential students to guide them to success Must possess the ability to maintain effective, cooperative working relationships with supervisors and co-workers in keeping with the values and mission of both the Department and the University Must possess above average oral, written, and computer communication skills and practice ethical decision making Must demonstrate willingness to role model acceptance and advocacy of diverse student populations by promoting a living and working environment committed to valuing diversity and social justice Must be willing to serve as a role model for residential students, student staff members, and co-workers in work ethic, attitude, and approach to work Must demonstrate an understanding of supervision of student staff members Must be willing to work evenings and high-volume weekends, and assume additional responsibilities within the department as needed Must reside in a designated professional staff apartment within the assigned residence hall for the duration of employment with Housing and Residence Life. This is a live-in position; the Residence Hall Director is required to reside in a designated professional staff apartment within the assigned residence hall for the duration of their employment with Housing and Residence Life at WKU. Although the majority of the position will function as described, some aspects are subject to change due to evolving departmental needs. Requirements: Bachelor's degree At least one (1) year previous experience as a Hall Director, Resident Assistant, Community Advisor, or other housing/residence life related leadership role Additional Information: Salary:  $43,896 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Application Instructions: The following items must be submitted through this electronic talent management system: Cover Letter Resume You will receive email confirmation that your submission has been received. The candidate review process will generally begin as materials are received. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Western Kentucky University 1906 College Heights Blvd. Bowling Green, KY 42101"
    },
