      "title": "Students",
      "description": "Employment at WKU | Western Kentucky University Your browser does not support iframes. Warning! This page requires JavaScript to be enabled in order to function properly. It appears it is currently turned off for your browser. If you need help enabling JavaScript, please contact the ITS Service Desk . Skip to main content Western Kentucky University Apply Visit More Info About WKU Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Students Campus Safety Bookstore iWKU Mobile App Dining Transportation Faculty/Staff Academic Calendar Human Resources Directory Health & Wellness myWKU Parents Family Programs Parent & Family Portal Campus Safety Cost of Attendance Member Profile Alumni Alumni Association Alumni Events Make a Gift SpiritFunder WKU SPIRIT Sign in to access Email • Blackboard • TopNet * Search WKU What majors and programs are available at WKU? How do I apply for financial aid and scholarships? Where can I register for a campus tour? What housing options are available? How can I contact an academic advisor? Sign in to access Email • Blackboard • TopNet Make a Gift Employment Work at WKU WKU Human Resources Human Resources Careers Prospective Employees Career Opportunities Equal Employment Opportunity About WKU Relocating to Bowling Green Current Employees Working at WKU Benefits Employee Wellness & Benefits Work-Life Balance Retirement Family & Medical Leave Educational Benefits Vendors' Contact Info Perks & Discounts for Employees Pay Administration Employee Tools Employee Tools New to WKU Forms Holiday Calendar EPAFs Hiring Toolkit Hiring Process Interview Exchange Resources Background Check Request Employee Development Staff Onboarding C.L.I.M.B. Higher: Equipping for Success Performance Development Reflection and Goal Setting Staff Excellence Awards Training Calendar Policies HR Policies State & Federal Notices Contact Us HR Service Tickets Staff Directory Ombuds Officer Map + Directions Why Choose WKU? Western Kentucky University (WKU) is a student-centered, applied-research institution\n                        committed to providing its students with a transformative academic and social experience\n                        and to elevating its surrounding communities.  Founded in 1906, WKU is the third largest\n                        public four-year institution in the Commonwealth of Kentucky with approximately 16,293\n                        students and nearly 2,612 faculty and staff employees*. Western Kentucky University is committed to empowering its campus community. At the\n                        heart of our mission, we seek to provide holistic education and employment experiences\n                        that prepare students, faculty, and staff to become effective scholars, contributors,\n                        and leaders in our ever-evolving communities. Located 65 miles north of Nashville, TN, and just over 100 miles south of Louisville,\n                        KY, WKU's main campus is in Bowling Green, KY - a city with approximately 70,000 residents.\n                        Our population is ethnically diverse, with more than 85 languages spoken in and around\n                        Bowling Green, and people from 35 nationalities call our community home. Western Kentucky University seeks to attract talented faculty and staff who are inspired\n                        individually to contribute to WKU's strategic plans and ongoing success. We offer\n                        comprehensive wellness and health benefits to employees and their families, including\n                        domestic partners and other qualified dependents and take pride in providing a workplace\n                        culture that supports balancing the responsibilities of work and family life. Paid-time\n                        off for holidays, vacation and sick leave, and a tuition discount program for employees\n                        and dependents are also provided. Learn more about WKU and Bowling Green at wku.edu/about . *Spring 2025 data; updated annually Returning Applicant Login Show Filters Categories Faculty Faculty (Part Time) Staff Temporary/Time Limited Clear Category Filters Locations Bowling Green, KY Elizabethtown, KY Elizabethtown/Fort Knox, KY Elizabethtown/Ft. Knox, KY Glasgow, KY Owensboro, KY Somerset, KY Clear Location Filters Sort By Date Posted (Newest) Date Posted (Oldest) Relevant Apply Filter Search Search Director, Budget and Finance - Housing and Residence Life Department: VP for Finance and Administration Posted On: Aug, 24th 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Staff Show Job Details for Director, Budget and Finance - Housing and Residence Life Apply Now for Director, Budget and Finance - Housing and Residence Life Position Summary: The Director, Budget and Finance - Housing and Residence Life is responsible for managing the financial operations of a comprehensive housing program consisting of 14 residence halls and 3 apartment complexes with a capacity of approximately 4,700 students. The position oversees all financial operations of Housing and Residence Life, including accounting, budgeting, forecasting, financial analysis, financial reporting, and compliance requirements. Western Kentucky University recently entered a public-private partnership (P3) with Gilbane Development Company and Inwood Management to improve the university's residential portfolio. The Director has a dual reporting line to the university's AVP for Budget, Finance and Analytics and AVP of Student Engagement and Executive Director of Housing and Residence Life, with responsibilities evolving to support the partnership. Primary Job Duties and Responsibilities: Financial Management Oversee month-end and year-end close, including financial statement preparation and account reconciliations. Ensure the accuracy and completeness of financial records, including the general ledger, accounts payable and receivable, payroll, fixed assets, and related financial systems. Coordinate with external partners, auditors, and other financial service providers to ensure compliance with all financial reporting and regulatory requirements, including annual audits and other reporting requirements. Oversee financial obligations associated with master-leased properties, including the review, processing, and payment of expenses such as insurance premiums, utilities, and other property-related costs. Manage the Aramark Dining accounts in collaboration with the AVP for Student Engagement and the Resident District Manager. Assist the university's tax compliance accountant with the annual negotiation of property and liability insurance. Develop and implement financial policies and procedures that align with the organization's values and strategic goals.. Budgeting and Forecasting Lead the annual Housing and Residence Life budgeting process, collaborating closely with the AVP for Student Engagement and the Housing Leadership Team to develop realistic and achievable budgets. Monitor budget-to-actual performance and regularly communicate financial results, forecasts, risks, and opportunities to the AVP for Budget, Finance and Analytics, AVP for Student Engagement, Housing and Residence Life Leadership Team, and university financial staff. Develop and maintain financial forecasting models that support long-term planning and decision-making. Public-Private Partnership (P3) Serve as the primary financial liaison with the P3 partner, maintaining timely and effective communication regarding invoicing, payments, reconciliations, reporting, and other fiscal matters related to the partnership. Develop, implement, and maintain financial controls and reporting processes related to P3 operations that ensure accountability, transparency, and compliance with university policies and contractual requirements. Oversee invoicing for reimbursable expenses and monitor accounts receivable related to the P3 partnership, ensuring accuracy and compliance with contractual agreements, as well as the timely collection of payments. Direct and monitor the timely reconciliation and transfer of housing revenues generated through the P3 arrangement, collaborating with the Director of Housing Operations to ensure accurate reporting and compliance with agreements. Secondary Job Duties and Responsibilities: Prepare ad hoc financial reports and analysis as needed. Serve as liaison with university departments on campus such as accounting, payroll, student billing, and student employment. Train current and new staff on university purchasing, pro-card, and web time-entry processes and guidelines. Track and reconcile expenditures and balances for WKU College Heights Foundation endowment accounts. Leadership Activities: Serve on the Housing and Residence Life Leadership Team. Participate in enrollment management and budget meetings with the AVP for Budget, Finance and Analytics and AVP of Student Engagement to support the annual budget. Create budgeting and purchasing presentations. Job Requirements: Bachelor's degree in accounting, finance, or a related field. At least 5 years of financial management experience, with knowledge of general ledger, financial statement reporting, and budgetary procedures and practices. Additional Information: Salary Range:  $75,000 - $90,000 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Steam System Technician I Department: Facilities Management Posted On: Aug, 18th 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Staff Show Job Details for Steam System Technician I Apply Now for Steam System Technician I Under general supervision of the Central Heating Plant Supervisor, the Steam System Technician performs skilled work at the experienced trade level in the maintenance and repair of boilers, repair of pumps, fans and compressors, as well as being responsible for the steam distribution system campus wide. Operate or tend steam distribution systems, boilers, and auxiliary equipment such as pumps, compressors, and related equipment, to supply and maintain steam or heat for University buildings Observe and interpret readings on gauges, meters, and charts registering various aspects of boiler operation to ensure that boilers are operating properly Monitor and inspect equipment, computer terminals, switches, valves, gauges, alarms, safety devices, and meters to detect leaks or malfunctions and to ensure that equipment is operating efficiently and safely Analyze problems and take appropriate action to ensure continuous and reliable operation of equipment and systems Maintain daily logs of operation, maintenance, and safety activities, including test results, instrument readings, and details of equipment malfunctions and maintenance work Assemble or secure pipes, tubes, fittings, or related equipment, according to specifications, by welding, brazing, cementing, soldering, or threading joints Turn valves to shut off steam, water, or other gases or liquids from pipe sections, using valve keys or wrenches Remove and replace worn components Examine boilers, pressure vessels, tanks, or vats to locate defects, such as leaks, weak spots, or defective sections, so that they can be repaired Inspect assembled vessels or individual components, such as tubes, fittings, valves, controls, or auxiliary mechanisms, to locate any defects Repair or replace defective pressure vessel parts, such as safety valves or regulators, using torches, jacks, caulking hammers, power saws, threading dies, welding equipment, or metalworking machinery Install manholes, handholes, taps, tubes, valves, gauges, or feedwater connections in drums of water tube and fire tube boilers, using hand tools Study blueprints to determine locations, relationships, or dimensions of parts Straighten or reshape metal parts, using hammers, jacks, or torches Other general maintenance to include: disassembling machinery or equipment to remove parts and make repairs, reassemble equipment after completion of inspections, testing or repairs Clean, lubricate or adjust parts, equipment or machinery Test boiler water quality or arrange for testing and take necessary corrective action, such as adding chemicals to prevent corrosion and harmful deposits Activate valves to maintain required amounts of water in boilers, to adjust supplies of combustion air, and to control the flow of fuel into burners Maintains excellent communication/customer service with Building Coordinators and all other DFM Supervisors Communicates bi-laterally with other DFM team members to coordinate work activities between groups Performs other duties as required Knowledge and Skills Essential for Success Mechanical & operational knowledge of all machines & tools related to steam and hot water equipment Troubleshooting skills to determine causes of operating errors and deciding what to do about it Skill to repair machines or systems using the needed tools Skill to perform routine maintenance on equipment and determine when and what kind of maintenance is needed Ability to provide on-the-job training/coaching to other steam system technicians regarding proper maintenance of boilers and steam distribution systems Ability to use logic and reasoning to identify the strengths and weaknesses of alternative solutions, conclusions or approaches to problems Ability to read and interpret blueprints, specification sheets, schematics, etc. Ability to monitor and assess performance of yourself and make improvements or take corrective action Ability to talk to others and convey information effectively Ability to manage one's own time effectively and efficiently Being reliable, responsible, dependable and able to fulfill obligations Being careful about detail and thorough in completing work tasks Ability to accept criticism and react calmly and effectively with high stress situations Possess basic computer skills, familiar with web/internet navigation, and willingness to learn and utilize new technology based products as applicable Adhere to all University policies and regulations Physical Abilities Required Installation skills for installing equipment, machines, wiring, or programs to meet specifications Ability to bend, crawl, reach, kneel, climb ladders & scaffolding, and able to navigate tight/confined spaces, as well as working in hot, noisy mechanical rooms Must be able to perform strenuous physical labor, which includes heavy lifting, carrying 50 lbs. or more on a regular basis Requires working outdoors in all types of weather conditions Must be able to wear protective eye wear, gloves, ear wear and top of head during work times for one's Job Requirements: High school diploma or GED Ability to bend, crawl, reach, kneel, climb ladders & scaffolding, and able to navigate tight/confined spaces, as well as working in hot, noisy mechanical rooms Must be able to perform strenuous physical labor, which includes heavy lifting, carrying 50 lbs. or more on a regular basis Requires working outdoors in all types of weather conditions Must be able to wear protective eye wear, gloves, ear wear and top of head during work times for one's safety as the task dictates Additional Information: Hourly Range:  $23.64-$25.78 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Specialist, Digital Media Content Department: Public Affairs Posted On: Aug, 12th 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Staff Show Job Details for Specialist, Digital Media Content Apply Now for Specialist, Digital Media Content The Digital Media Content Specialist supports marketing and communication efforts, focusing primarily on social media and digital content development for the website and other platforms. This role reports to the Assistant Director for Marketing Communications. In this service-oriented role, the successful candidate will monitor user activity, interpret and analyze engagement and performance, and respond accordingly. Primary Duties and Responsibilities: The following duties are customary for this position, but are not to be construed as all-inclusive. Duties may be added, deleted and assigned based on management discretion and institutional needs. Create content and provide support for social media campaigns, marketing campaigns, institutional weather and crisis communication plans, written features, university events, and other official university communications. Develop and manage content calendar across institutional social media platforms to support the university's strategic plan, drive engagement, attract prospective students, and retain current students. Establish and maintain collaborative partnerships with University Marketing staff and key university stakeholders (e.g. academic college content coordinators) on writing, photography, videography, and digital graphics projects. Evaluate overall campaign performance, identify opportunities to evolve the marketing strategy, and implement SEO, accessibility, and content optimization strategies. Utilize social listening to monitor brand mentions and deliver customer service. Provide consultations, audits, and plan/campaign development assistance for campus offices in matters of social media marketing. Work closely with student interns, student social media ambassadors, or similar student support to implement the University's content strategies. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Considered Essential for Success: Ability to plan, schedule, and prioritize work activities and assignments to ensure efficiency and effectiveness in meeting deadlines, along with the ability to multi-task. Exhibit strong interpersonal communication skills, including excellent listening, written, and verbal abilities, to work effectively with individuals across varying roles and experiences. Possess computer literacy and proficiency, including the Microsoft Office Suite, Canva, and Adobe Acrobat. Demonstrate the ability to execute tasks, collaborate effectively, communicate professionally, and adapt to stressful environments or sudden changes in tasks with limited notice. Possess hands-on experience with content creation for social media platforms (e.g. Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn, YouTube, etc.) Possess social media listening skills, decision making and problem-solving skills, and judgement to identify and monitor crisis situations. Ability to utilize a smartphone to capture photo and video content. Ability to spend specific periods of time at a computer workstation. Able to travel and work in standard office conditions. Job Requirements: Bachelor's degree Experience managing social media in a professional environment Experience writing for the web and/or developing digital content Additional Information: Salary:  $46,100 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Trauma Clinician, LCCWEAR Integrated Family Trauma Treatment Clinic Department: Dean CHHS Posted On: Aug, 6th 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Staff Show Job Details for Trauma Clinician, LCCWEAR Integrated Family Trauma Treatment Clinic Apply Now for Trauma Clinician, LCCWEAR Integrated Family Trauma Treatment Clinic Western Kentucky University's LifeSkills Center for Child Welfare Education and Research (LCCWEAR) is seeking applications for the Integrated Family Trauma Treatment Clinic Trauma Clinician.  The Trauma Clinician will provide evidence-based trauma therapy, case management, and systemic advocacy/collaboration for children, adults, and families and therapeutic services will include therapy, comprehensive trauma assessment, ongoing reassessment and screening, and education. Non-therapeutic interventions to include case management, referrals, service follow up, and parenting education. Additionally, the trauma clinician will assist in the development and facilitation of a systemic intervention intended to prevent out of home placement of children involved in the child welfare system and will report to the Clinic Manager of the IFTTC. The Trauma Clinician will have an ability to establish priorities and work independently to meet deadlines, be organized and detail oriented with the capacity to work in a busy environment with frequent interruption, and maintain the highest standards of professionalism, integrity, accountability, cooperation, and customer service. Also, they will demonstrate computer literacy and proficiency to include Microsoft Office Suite and have excellent listening, written, and verbal communication skills. The Trauma Clinician will possess strong decision making, problem solving, and organizational skills and strong interpersonal communication skills with an ability to work with a wide spectrum of individuals in a diverse setting. The following duties are expected for this position but are not to be construed as all-inclusive.  Duties may be added, deleted, and assigned based on management discretion and institutional needs. Provide evidence-based or evidence-informed trauma-specific therapy services Maintain an ongoing caseload with children and parents involved in the child welfare system, completing detailed documentation of service delivery Deliver therapy, case management, and systemic collaboration services Contribute to development, design, and facilitation of learning collaborative for child welfare intervention Participate in and co-facilitate multidisciplinary case consultation for families involved with the child welfare system Maintain ongoing communication and collaboration with network of community partners, including Kentucky's Cabinet for Health and Family Services, to enhance the provision of services This is a grant funded position. Continuation is dependent upon funding/need. Job Requirements: Master's degree in social work, psychology, or clinical counseling Independent licensure in the state of Kentucky Trained and certified in Trauma Focused Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (TF-CBT) or working toward certification At least 2 years of experience in evidence based or evidence informed trauma treatment Additional Information: Salary: $61,200 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Assistant Director, Student Success Analytics and Engagement Technologies Department: Student Development & Engagement Posted On: Aug, 4th 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Staff Show Job Details for Assistant Director, Student Success Analytics and Engagement Technologies Apply Now for Assistant Director, Student Success Analytics and Engagement Technologies The Assistant Director of Student Success Analytics and Engagement Technologies serves as a key leader in advancing Western Kentucky University's student success, retention, and engagement initiatives through the effective implementation, utilization, and assessment of enterprise student success technologies, to ensure data-informed practices. Reporting to the Assistant Provost for Student Success and Online Learning, this position provides operational leadership, analytics support, and campus coordination for WKU's academic advising, student development and engagement, and academic support and recovery platforms. The Assistant Director works collaboratively across Academic Affairs, Student Affairs, Enrollment Management, Academic Advising, Career Development, and Academic Support and Retention Programs to promote adoption of student success technologies, build institutional capacity for data-informed decision-making, and ensure campus stakeholders effectively leverage analytics and engagement data to improve student outcomes. This position combines expertise in analytics, project implementation, change management, training, and stakeholder engagement to maximize institutional return on investment in student success technologies and support WKU's strategic priorities related to retention, persistence, student development, and post-graduation success. Primary Responsibilities Support the effective utilization and continuous improvement of the Civitas Learning Student Impact Platform and Suitable by serving as the primary operational resource for campus users. Coordinate training, onboarding, and professional development opportunities for faculty, staff, advisors, and student success professionals to increase proficiency and adoption of student success technologies. Develop user guides, resource materials, and communication strategies that promote consistent and effective platform use across academic and student support units. Monitor platform utilization, identify opportunities to increase engagement and adoption, and recommend strategies to improve participation among campus stakeholders. Serve as a liaison between platform users and institutional leadership by gathering feedback, identifying challenges, and communicating enhancement opportunities. Collaborate with campus partners to integrate student success technologies into advising, retention, academic support, career development, and student engagement workflows. Analyze platform dashboards, reports, and engagement data to identify emerging trends, opportunities, and areas of concern affecting student success outcomes. Provide actionable insights and recommendations to the Assistant Provost for Student Success and Online Learning and campus stakeholders to support data-informed decision-making and continuous improvement initiatives. Evaluate the effectiveness of technology-enabled interventions and student success initiatives through ongoing assessment and analysis. Support implementation of new platform features, enhancements, and institutional initiatives designed to improve student engagement, persistence, retention, and completion. Develop, maintain, and disseminate dashboards, reports, and visualizations that communicate student success, retention, persistence, engagement, and intervention outcomes to campus stakeholders. Coordinate analyses of key Civitas capabilities including Student Outcome Analytics, Predictive Factors of Course Success, Initiative Analysis, Course Insights, and Course Demand Analytics. Monitor student participation, engagement activity completion, and digital badge attainment within Suitable, and provide reports that inform institutional engagement and student development initiatives. In collaboration with the Assistant Provost for Student Success and Online Learning, facilitate campus adoption of student success technologies through stakeholder engagement, consultation, and change management strategies that support sustainable integration into institutional workflows. Job Requirements: Master's degree in Higher Education Administration, Educational Leadership, Data Analytics, Information Systems, Student Affairs, Business Analytics, or a related field. Four years of progressively responsible experience in student success, advising, assessment, analytics, institutional research, educational technology, or related fields. Experience utilizing data to inform decision-making and improve organizational outcomes. Experience developing reports, dashboards, or assessment tools. Additional Information: Salary:  $57,720 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Network Engineer Department: Infrastructure & Ops - Network Posted On: Jul, 29th 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Staff Show Job Details for Network Engineer Apply Now for Network Engineer Purpose of the Position Western Kentucky University is seeking a highly motivated Network Engineer to join the Network Team within the Infrastructure and Operations Department. This position plays a key role in designing, implementing, maintaining, and advancing the University's enterprise network infrastructure that supports students, faculty, staff, research, and critical campus operations. Reporting to the Lead Network Engineer, this position works collaboratively with technology teams across the University to deliver reliable, secure, and innovative networking solutions. The successful candidate will contribute to strategic technology initiatives while supporting a complex environment that includes core, data center, wireless, edge, communications, and access network technologies. This is an excellent opportunity for a network professional who enjoys solving complex technical challenges, working with modern enterprise technologies from leading equipment providers like HPE(Aruba/Juniper), Cisco, and other top tier equipment, and making a meaningful impact within a large and diverse campus environment. Primary Duties and Responsibilities The following duties are representative of the position and are not intended to be all inclusive. Additional responsibilities may be assigned based on departmental and institutional needs. Network Engineering & Operations Design, implement, maintain, and troubleshoot enterprise network infrastructure supporting academic, administrative, residential, and research environments. Install, configure, and support enterprise-class network switches, routers, wireless systems, communications systems, and related technologies. Monitor and optimize network performance, availability, reliability, and security. Participate in the planning and implementation of network upgrades, expansions, and modernization initiatives. Maintain accurate network documentation, diagrams, standards, and operational procedures. Support and maintain network management, monitoring, authentication, and security systems. Technical Leadership & Collaboration Provide technical guidance and mentorship to Network Specialists and other technical staff. Collaborate with internal ITS teams and campus stakeholders to support technology initiatives and institutional objectives. Research emerging technologies and evaluate solutions that enhance network performance, security, and operational efficiency. Participate in project planning, coordination, and execution for network and enterprise technology projects. Support & Service Provide exceptional customer service while supporting faculty, staff, students, and departmental technology partners. Participate in a rotating on-call schedule to support planned maintenance activities and respond to critical network incidents when necessary. Maintain flexibility to perform occasional work outside normal business hours to support project implementations and emergency response activities. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities The successful candidate will demonstrate: A strong commitment to customer service and technical excellence. Exceptional attention to detail and organizational skills. A collaborative mindset with the ability to build productive working relationships across technical and non-technical teams. A passion for continuous learning and professional development. The ability to communicate complex technical concepts clearly to audiences of varying technical backgrounds. Professionalism, integrity, accountability, and commitment to supporting the University's mission. Strong analytical, troubleshooting, and problem-solving skills. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to manage projects and prioritize multiple responsibilities. Experience supporting enterprise wireless networking environments. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment. Operational familiarity with Linux, Windows Server, VMware ESX, and x86/x64 server platforms Job Requirements: Bachelor's Degree Minimum of three years of relevant professional experience in network engineering, network administration, or a closely related field. Experience deploying, configuring, and supporting enterprise networking technologies. Experience with Aruba/Juniper/Cisco and/or other leading enterprise networking platforms. Experience using network monitoring, management, and documentation systems within a large-scale environment. Working knowledge of Ethernet, IP, VLAN, SNMP, DNS, DHCP, and VoIP technologies. Valid driver's license maintained in accordance with university requirements. Additional Information: Salary Range: $ 70,000 - $75,000 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Director, Regional Campuses (Internal Search) Department: Provost/VP Academic Affairs Posted On: Jul, 29th 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Staff Show Job Details for Director, Regional Campuses (Internal Search) Apply Now for Director, Regional Campuses (Internal Search) Internal Search: only WKU employees currently working in a non-temporary status are eligible to apply. The Director, Regional Campuses will provide oversight to the regional campuses on a daily basis as a direct report to the Associate Provost for Faculty and Academic Excellence. The Director will be expected to supervise the staff for the current regional campus locations, collaborate with Academic Colleges and Departments to provide strategic planning for instruction and programs to meet the unique needs within each community, and oversee the daily duties of operating regional campus locations. The regional campus locations include Elizabethtown, Ft. Knox, Glasgow, Somerset, and Owensboro. The successful candidate for Director, Regional Campuses must be knowledgeable about and focused on the students, constituents and communities served by the WKU Regional Campuses, including the development of academic and student focused programming, maintenance of physical buildings and grounds, and development of strong community relationships. This is a full-time, twelve-month position. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Provide supervision for approximately 13 full-time staff, including evaluations, personnel hiring, development, and goal setting Provide strategic direction for program development in collaboration with Colleges and Departments to meet the needs of the regional students Provide leadership in developing community relationships and other regionally located institutional partners at each of the regional locations Manage the Regional Campuses' annual budget and provide financial oversight, including monitoring and balancing budgetary expenses. Ensure the physical environment at each location facilitates safety and learning for students, staff, faculty, and clients including strategies and oversight for both physical plant and technology. This includes the offices at Elizabethtown, Ft. Knox, and Somerset, and the buildings and grounds at Glasgow and Owensboro. Under the direction of the Associate Provost for Faculty and Academic Excellence, provide leadership to provide excellent academic support services to regional students at all off-campus instructional sites under the regional campus umbrella, including the Early College Program in Glasgow. Develop and implement effective initiatives that will further WKU's mission to serve this region. This will include working with Enrollment and Student Experience offices to support recruitment and retention efforts for transfer and regional students. Job Requirements: Master's Degree Demonstrated strong leadership skills Good organizational, planning, and coordination skills Demonstrated ability to multi-task and re-prioritize as needed Must demonstrate strong knowledge of WKU programs and regional education particular to the WKU Regional Campuses Strong interpersonal skills and ability to build collaborative relationships Good verbal presentation, group dynamic, and facilitation skills Demonstrated supervisory experience Demonstrated ability to develop effective operating procedures and long-range plans Demonstrated ability to champion regional campus strengths and needs to a variety of constituencies including political representatives, educational boards, and the general public Must possess valid Kentucky driver's license Ability to spend significant periods of time at a computer workstation Ability to travel between regional campus locations Additional Information: Salary Range: $80,000 - $95,000 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Specialist, Retention Programs & Academic Support Department: Student Development & Engagement Posted On: Jul, 29th 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Staff Show Job Details for Specialist, Retention Programs & Academic Support Apply Now for Specialist, Retention Programs & Academic Support The Specialist, Retention Programs & Academic Support supports the coordination of academic support and retention initiatives. This position assists with programs and services designed to help students transition successfully to WKU, respond to academic difficulty, connect with academic support resources, and persist toward good academic standing. The position provides operational support for retention initiatives such as the Academic Recovery & Support Program, Summer Scholars academic support, and peer coaching / Peer Assisted Study Sessions (PASS) connections. The Specialist works collaboratively with campus partners to help students understand expectations, identify support needs, and connect with resources that promote academic success. Primary Responsibilities Coordinate day-to-day support for retention and academic support initiatives, including the Academic Recovery & Support Program (Best Expectation Program (BEP) formerly) and Summer Scholars academic support. Assist students in understanding academic standing, academic recovery expectations, peer coaching / PASS services, and available campus resources. Teach up to 6 hours of college coursework. Support student communication, workshop logistics, attendance tracking, completion records, and follow-up for assigned programs. Connect students to peer services, PASS, advising, financial aid, wellness resources, faculty support, and other campus partners as appropriate. Support the coordination, training, scheduling, and supervision of assigned peer coaches, PASS leaders, or student employees. Assist with development and maintenance of program materials, student-facing resources, webpages, forms, and communication templates. Support tracking and reporting related to participation, completion, student engagement, resource referrals, and academic recovery outcomes. Collaborate with academic advising, faculty, academic colleges, Registrar, Financial Aid, Housing and Residence Life, TRIO, Intercultural Student Engagement Center, and other student success partners. Support continuous improvement of academic support and retention programs through student feedback, data review, and program assessment. Provide occasional evening or weekend support for workshops, summer programming, or student success activities as needed. Job Requirements: Master's degree. Experience supporting students, academic support programs, retention initiatives, peer coaching, advising, or related student success work. Strong organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities, communicate clearly with students and campus partners, and maintain accurate program records. Commitment to supporting students from diverse backgrounds and experiences. Additional Information: Salary: $43,888 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Part-time Police Officer, Glasgow Campus Department: Police Posted On: Jul, 23rd 2026 Location: Glasgow, KY Category: Staff Show Job Details for Part-time Police Officer, Glasgow Campus Apply Now for Part-time Police Officer, Glasgow Campus Provide a presence on the Glasgow campus Monday thru Thursday from 8:00 am to 11:30 am. Conduct Criminal and Accident investigations on campus as well adhering to clery reporting laws. Assessable and maintain a positive relationship with staff and students during his/her tour of duty. Other duties as assigned. Job Requirements: HS Diploma or GED Police Officer must be have the Peace Officer Professional Standard certification. Must pass the WKU Police Department  background check. Additional Information: Hourly Rate: $32.00 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Assistant Research Hydrologist Department: Crawford Hydrology Lab Posted On: Jul, 23rd 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Staff Show Job Details for Assistant Research Hydrologist Apply Now for Assistant Research Hydrologist Western Kentucky University (WKU) is seeking a highly organized and technically skilled Assistant Research Hydrologist to serve as Lab Manager for the Crawford Hydrology Laboratory (CHL). CHL is a nationally and internationally recognized leader in groundwater flow investigations, specializing in advanced fluorescent dye tracing techniques within karst landscape and aquifer systems. The ideal candidate will manage day-to-day laboratory operations, oversee quality assurance programs, supervise student employees, assist with field investigations. Job Requirements: Master's degree in Geosciences, Hydrology, Environmental Science, Biology, Chemistry, or a closely related STEM discipline. Demonstrated experience working in an analytical laboratory environment. Familiarity with laboratory instrumentation, data analysis software, and standard scientific quality control protocols. Strong technical writing abilities and excellent interpersonal communication for client and university relations. Additional Information: Hourly Range:  $24.62 - $25.64 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Sectio