      "description": "Employment at WKU | Western Kentucky University Your browser does not support iframes. Warning! This page requires JavaScript to be enabled in order to function properly. It appears it is currently turned off for your browser. If you need help enabling JavaScript, please contact the ITS Service Desk . Skip to main content Western Kentucky University Apply Visit More Info About WKU Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Students Campus Safety Bookstore iWKU Mobile App Dining Transportation Faculty/Staff Academic Calendar Human Resources Directory Health & Wellness myWKU Parents Family Programs Parent & Family Portal Campus Safety Cost of Attendance Member Profile Alumni Alumni Association Alumni Events Make a Gift SpiritFunder WKU SPIRIT Sign in to access Email • Blackboard • TopNet * Search WKU What majors and programs are available at WKU? How do I apply for financial aid and scholarships? Where can I register for a campus tour? What housing options are available? How can I contact an academic advisor? Sign in to access Email • Blackboard • TopNet Make a Gift Employment Work at WKU WKU Human Resources Human Resources Careers Prospective Employees Career Opportunities Equal Employment Opportunity About WKU Relocating to Bowling Green Current Employees Working at WKU Benefits Employee Wellness & Benefits Work-Life Balance Retirement Family & Medical Leave Educational Benefits Vendors' Contact Info Perks & Discounts for Employees Pay Administration Employee Tools Employee Tools New to WKU Forms Holiday Calendar EPAFs Hiring Toolkit Hiring Process Interview Exchange Resources Background Check Request Employee Development Staff Onboarding C.L.I.M.B. Higher: Equipping for Success Performance Development Reflection and Goal Setting Staff Excellence Awards Training Calendar Policies HR Policies State & Federal Notices Contact Us HR Service Tickets Staff Directory Ombuds Officer Map + Directions Why Choose WKU? Western Kentucky University (WKU) is a student-centered, applied-research institution\n                        committed to providing its students with a transformative academic and social experience\n                        and to elevating its surrounding communities.  Founded in 1906, WKU is the third largest\n                        public four-year institution in the Commonwealth of Kentucky with approximately 16,293\n                        students and nearly 2,612 faculty and staff employees*. Western Kentucky University is committed to empowering its campus community. At the\n                        heart of our mission, we seek to provide holistic education and employment experiences\n                        that prepare students, faculty, and staff to become effective scholars, contributors,\n                        and leaders in our ever-evolving communities. Located 65 miles north of Nashville, TN, and just over 100 miles south of Louisville,\n                        KY, WKU's main campus is in Bowling Green, KY - a city with approximately 70,000 residents.\n                        Our population is ethnically diverse, with more than 85 languages spoken in and around\n                        Bowling Green, and people from 35 nationalities call our community home. Western Kentucky University seeks to attract talented faculty and staff who are inspired\n                        individually to contribute to WKU's strategic plans and ongoing success. We offer\n                        comprehensive wellness and health benefits to employees and their families, including\n                        domestic partners and other qualified dependents and take pride in providing a workplace\n                        culture that supports balancing the responsibilities of work and family life. Paid-time\n                        off for holidays, vacation and sick leave, and a tuition discount program for employees\n                        and dependents are also provided. Learn more about WKU and Bowling Green at wku.edu/about . *Spring 2025 data; updated annually Returning Applicant Login Show Filters Categories Faculty Faculty (Part Time) Staff Temporary/Time Limited Clear Category Filters Locations Bowling Green, KY Elizabethtown, KY Elizabethtown/Fort Knox, KY Elizabethtown/Ft. Knox, KY Glasgow, KY Owensboro, KY Somerset, KY Clear Location Filters Sort By Date Posted (Newest) Date Posted (Oldest) Relevant Apply Filter Search Search Faculty (Part-time) - Entrepreneurship Department: Management Posted On: Jul, 9th 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Faculty (Part Time) Show Job Details for Faculty (Part-time) - Entrepreneurship Apply Now for Faculty (Part-time) - Entrepreneurship The Gordon Ford College of Business is accepting applications to create a pool of qualified faculty to teach graduate and undergraduate courses in Entrepreneurship. We are seeking part time faculty for day, evening and online classes at the main campus location. Job Requirements: A master's degree in the discipline (or closely related field) is required for teaching undergraduate-level courses; a terminal degree is required for teaching graduate-level courses. Prior teaching experience and experience with online education is desirable. Additional Information: Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, should notify the office of Institutional Equity. To request an accommodation, report a complaint, or ask questions regarding WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy (#0.2040), please contact Ms. Ena Demir, Executive Director/Title IX Coordinator via email at ena.demir@wku.edu or by phone at (270) 745-6867. Ms. Demir is also responsible for coordinating the University's response to complaints related to sex and gender harassment. Additional information regarding Title IX is accessible via WKU's https://www.wku.edu/titleix/ website. Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: http://www.wku.edu/atwku/academics.php For information related to job postings, please email employment@wku.edu . Faculty (Part-time)-Business Law/Legal Environment of Business Department: Management Posted On: Jul, 9th 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Faculty (Part Time) Show Job Details for Faculty (Part-time)-Business Law/Legal Environment of Business Apply Now for Faculty (Part-time)-Business Law/Legal Environment of Business The Gordon Ford College of Business is accepting applications to create a pool of qualified faculty to teach graduate and undergraduate courses in Business Law/Legal Environment of Business. We are seeking part time faculty for day, evening and online classes at the main campus location. Job Requirements: A master's degree in the discipline (or closely related field) is required for teaching undergraduate-level courses; a terminal degree is required for teaching graduate-level courses. Prior teaching experience and experience with online education is desirable. Additional Information: Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, should notify the office of Institutional Equity. To request an accommodation, report a complaint, or ask questions regarding WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy (#0.2040), please contact Ms. Ena Demir, Executive Director/Title IX Coordinator via email at ena.demir@wku.edu or by phone at (270) 745-6867. Ms. Demir is also responsible for coordinating the University's response to complaints related to sex and gender harassment. Additional information regarding Title IX is accessible via WKU's https://www.wku.edu/titleix/ website. Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: http://www.wku.edu/atwku/academics.php For information related to job postings, please email employment@wku.edu . Faculty (Part-time) - Analytics & Information Systems Department: Analytics & Information Systems Posted On: Jul, 9th 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Faculty (Part Time) Show Job Details for Faculty (Part-time) - Analytics & Information Systems Apply Now for Faculty (Part-time) - Analytics & Information Systems The Gordon Ford College of Business is accepting applications to create a pool of instructors for any current or future part-time assignments in Analytics & Information Systems . Course topics would be in one of the following areas: Analytics, Cybersecurity Analytics, and Artificial Intelligence. We are seeking part time faculty for day and evening classes at the main campus location. Job Requirements: A master's degree in the discipline (or closely related field) is required for teaching undergraduate-level courses; a terminal degree is required for teaching graduate-level courses. Prior teaching experience and experience with online education is desirable. Additional Information: Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, should notify the office of Institutional Equity. To request an accommodation, report a complaint, or ask questions regarding WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy (#0.2040), please contact Ms. Ena Demir, Executive Director/Title IX Coordinator via email at ena.demir@wku.edu or by phone at (270) 745-6867. Ms. Demir is also responsible for coordinating the University's response to complaints related to sex and gender harassment. Additional information regarding Title IX is accessible via WKU's https://www.wku.edu/titleix/ website. Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: http://www.wku.edu/atwku/academics.php For information related to job postings, please email employment@wku.edu . Assistant Director, Educational Outreach - Gatton Academy Department: Gatton Academy of Math and Science Posted On: Jun, 26th 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Staff Show Job Details for Assistant Director, Educational Outreach - Gatton Academy Apply Now for Assistant Director, Educational Outreach - Gatton Academy The Carol Martin Gatton Academy of Mathematics and Science in Kentucky seeks qualified candidates for the position of Assistant Director of Educational Outreach. The Gatton Academy is a public residential STEM program established and funded by the Kentucky legislature. It is located on the campus of Western Kentucky University. Students complete their last two years of high school in the program while earning at least 60 hours of college credit. This is a 12-month position and reports to the Director of The Gatton Academy. Gatton Academy staff and administrators are officially employees of Western Kentucky University. Primary Duties and Responsibilities The following duties are customary for this position but are not to be construed as all-inclusive.  Duties may be added, deleted, and assigned based on management discretion and institutional needs. Manage all aspects of the administration of The Gatton Academy's statewide educational outreach beyond the residential program. Develop a delivery system for online, synchronous, live courses such that students anywhere in the state may participate from their schools or homes. Ensure all courses meet accreditation requirements such that schools will award credit for students completing the courses. Build and maintain relationships with key representatives within the Kentucky Department of Education, school district personnel statewide, and key WKU personnel. Market educational outreach opportunities statewide. Establish and maintain a system for appropriately maintaining student records, documenting students' participation in and completion of courses. Establish and maintain clear communication channels with students, their families, and school personnel. Manage division budget. Implement, monitor, and assess functions of the division, including tracking annual performance indicators for division. Envision new programs, opportunities for growth, and refinement of services for division. Manage all aspects of the curriculum offered by The Gatton Academy through the educational outreach program. Oversee the curriculum development of courses designed specifically for advanced learners. Ensure students are provided with appropriate differentiation and support while taking courses. Supervise and support teachers who provide instruction within the educational outreach program. Recruit teachers to teach within the program. Ensure teachers meet state requirements to teach accredited courses. Provide training in effective instruction of advanced and gifted and talented learners. Develop a system to evaluate, provide feedback, and support teachers within the program. Provide direct support to students as a staff mentor/College Letter Writer, on study abroad programs, and as part of the Gatton leadership team. Perform other duties as assigned Knowledge and Skills Considered Essential for Success Understanding of gifted and talented students and their educational needs Excellent interpersonal skills Excellent communication skills Excellent organizational skills Compensation and Benefits 12-month contract paid over a 12-month period Salary range of $60,000 to $68,000 annually, with benefits package including options for medical insurance, dental insurance, life insurance, retirement plan (KTRS or ORT), partial University tuition waiver, University Bookstore discount, and reduced-price membership to the University's health and fitness facility (Salary pay band 109) Job Requirements: Master's degree in Education or related field Experience teaching gifted and talented or high ability students Experience working with teachers of gifted and talented students Experience providing professional development for educators Additional Information: Salary Range:  $60,000 to $68,000 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Departmental Collaborative Pianist, Visiting Instructor Department: Music Posted On: Jun, 23rd 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Faculty Show Job Details for Departmental Collaborative Pianist, Visiting Instructor Apply Now for Departmental Collaborative Pianist, Visiting Instructor Western Kentucky University invites applications for the position of Departmental Collaborative Pianist, Visiting Instructor to begin in Fall 2026. This is a full-time, benefits-eligible, nine-month temporary appointment for the 2026-27 academic year. The Department of Music anticipates conducting a search for a permanent position during the 2026-27 academic year. The anticipated start date for this appointment is August 15, 2026. Applicants who meet the educational qualifications, requirements, and relevant experience are encouraged to apply. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Relevant professional collaborative piano experience. A high level of artistry demonstrated through excellent technical facility, outstanding sight-reading skill, the ability to learn music quickly, and knowledge of both instrumental and vocal repertoire. Demonstrated success in teaching and mentoring piano students in collaborative piano. Ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, and guest artists in a fast-paced academic environment. Exceptional communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to coordinate schedules, manage multiple requests, and maintain clear communication across the department. Responsibilities Exact duties to be assigned by the Department Chair and may include: Providing collaborative piano services for the music department, including student recitals, juries, applied lessons, rehearsals, studio classes, departmental auditions, and other departmental performances and events. Services may also include collaborating with faculty, guest artists, and ensembles. Serving as Coordinator of Collaborative Piano Services for the department, including managing intake of collaborative piano service requests, coordinating and distributing workload to part-time collaborative pianists, and maintaining communication with faculty and students regarding assignments and scheduling. Teaching collaborative piano/accompanying courses to piano majors. Working flexible hours in accordance with rehearsal and performance schedules. Other duties as assigned. Job Requirements: Earned advanced degree in collaborative piano, piano performance, or piano-related degree with an emphasis in collaborative piano by August 1, 2026. Master's degree Additional Information: Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Pedagogical Assistant/Associate/Professor of Counseling Department: Counseling and Student Affairs Posted On: Jun, 12th 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Faculty Show Job Details for Pedagogical Assistant/Associate/Professor of Counseling Apply Now for Pedagogical Assistant/Associate/Professor of Counseling The Department offers CACREP-accredited programs in Clinical Mental Health Counseling (both residential and digital pathways) and in Marriage, Couple, and Family Counseling; Graduate Certificate programs in Addictions Education; and a graduate degree program in Student Affairs. Additionally, the department houses the Talley Family Counseling Center (TFCC), an onsite counseling training center. Please visit http://www.wku.edu/csa/ for more information. This tenure eligible position includes teaching and service responsibilities. The candidate selected for the position will be expected to provide outstanding instruction, as well as activity in collegial and professional service. Teaching will be in person on the main campus and will begin August 2026. Job Requirements: Requirements for all levels include: a doctorate from a CACREP-accredited counselor education and supervision program; experience as a Professional Counselor, eligibility for Licensed Professional Clinical Counselor (LPCC) credential in Kentucky. Additionally, they should be familiar in the history of participation in relevant professional organizations and demonstration of success or potential success in teaching. Appointment at Associate Professor must include tenure and promotion earned as a faculty member within a CACREP-accredited program and as consistent with WKU's Criteria for Individual Ranks (WKU Faculty Handbook, 31st ed., III.C.1.a.). Appointment at Professor must include tenure and promotion earned as a faculty member within a CACREP-accredited program and as consistent with WKU's Criteria for Individual Ranks (WKU Faculty Handbook, 31st ed., III.C.1.a.); must demonstrate and provide evidence of strong levels of performance across teaching, and university/public service throughout tenure at Professor rank. Additional Information: Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, should notify the office of Institutional Equity. To request an accommodation, report a complaint, or ask questions regarding WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy (#0.2040), please contact Ms. Ena Demir, Executive Director/Title IX Coordinator via email at ena.demir@wku.edu or by phone at (270) 745-6867. Ms. Demir is also responsible for coordinating the University's response to complaints related to sex and gender harassment. Additional information regarding Title IX is accessible via WKU's https://www.wku.edu/titleix/ website. Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: http://www.wku.edu/atwku/academics.php For information related to job postings, please email employment@wku.edu . Instructor I, School of Nursing and Allied Health Department: School of Nursing and Allied Health Posted On: May, 29th 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Faculty Show Job Details for Instructor I, School of Nursing and Allied Health Apply Now for Instructor I, School of Nursing and Allied Health The School of Nursing and Allied Health is seeking candidates for a full-time Instructor (9-month) position for the online LPN to ASN Program with an August 15, 2026, start date. Qualified applicants have expertise in adult Medical Surgical/Critical Care Nursing. Job Requirements: Minimum of a Master's Degree in Nursing. Maintain active, unencumbered Kentucky or compact state RN and/or APRN licensure, and meet any additional requirements as required by clinical agencies (which may include but is not limited to: Immunizations, titers, liability insurance, CPR, TB screening, and annual influenza vaccination). The cost of meeting the clinical agency requirements is at the expense of the faculty. Minimum of two-years of acute care medical surgical/critical care nursing practice within the last five years (or) recent medical surgical/critical care clinical teaching experience. Candidates must be able to teach in classroom, lab and clinical settings as assigned. Additional Information: Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, should notify the office of Institutional Equity. To request an accommodation, report a complaint, or ask questions regarding WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy (#0.2040), please contact Ms. Ena Demir, Executive Director/Title IX Coordinator via email at ena.demir@wku.edu or by phone at (270) 745-6867. Ms. Demir is also responsible for coordinating the University's response to complaints related to sex and gender harassment. Additional information regarding Title IX is accessible via WKU's https://www.wku.edu/titleix/ website. Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: http://www.wku.edu/atwku/academics.php For information related to job postings, please email employment@wku.edu . Facilitator (WKU in Owensboro) Department: WKU - Owensboro Posted On: May, 27th 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Staff Show Job Details for Facilitator (WKU in Owensboro) Apply Now for Facilitator (WKU in Owensboro) Facilitators arrive before assigned classes, are available throughout the classes, and stay until all students depart the classroom. Facilitators are responsible for readying and monitoring Connect (Zoom, classroom) technology for instruction, including working with the WKU IT HelpDesk to solve any problems that arise. The position is responsible for routine communication with the instructor of record (faculty) who will be in a different WKU location via email, phone, and Zoom technology. Facilitators may also answer phones for the campus and greet all campus visitors. The position is responsible for classroom closing procedures. Primary Duties and Responsibilities: Provide support and assistance to Connect course students and facilitators, including arriving at assigned Connect courses 30 minutes before class time, having all equipment operational by beginning of classes Troubleshooting equipment and work through problems with WKU IT HelpDesk staff Assists instructors with classroom assignments, copying and distributing materials, accepting student work and sending it to correct location, and proctoring exams. Secure and straighten all classrooms after vacated and close and secure the building when all evening classes have ended Greet all WKU students, staff, faculty, and other members of the community upon entry to the campus Answer incoming phone calls and direct them to the proper resource Assists with office duties as assigned Job Requirements: High school diploma or GED Additional Information: Hourly Rate:  $13.00 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, should notify the office of Institutional Equity. To request an accommodation, report a complaint, or ask questions regarding WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy (#0.2040), please contact Ms. Ena Demir, Executive Director/Title IX Coordinator via email at ena.demir@wku.edu or by phone at (270) 745-6867. Ms. Demir is also responsible for coordinating the University's response to complaints related to sex and gender harassment. Additional information regarding Title IX is accessible via WKU's https://www.wku.edu/titleix/ website. Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: http://www.wku.edu/atwku/academics.php For information related to job postings, please email employment@wku.edu . Clinical Assistant Professor, School of Nursing Allied Health Department: School of Nursing and Allied Health Posted On: May, 20th 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Faculty Show Job Details for Clinical Assistant Professor, School of Nursing Allied Health Apply Now for Clinical Assistant Professor, School of Nursing Allied Health The School of Nursing and Allied Health is seeking candidates for a full-time Clinical Assistant Professor (9-month) position for the BSN Program with an August 17, 2026, start date. Qualified applicants have expertise in adult and/or pediatric Medical Surgical Nursing. Job Requirements: Minimum of a Master's Degree in Nursing. Maintain active, unencumbered Kentucky or compact state RN and/or APRN licensure, and meet any additional requirements as required by clinical agencies (which may include but is not limited to: Immunizations, titers, liability insurance, CPR, TB screening, and annual influenza vaccination). The cost of meeting the clinical agency requirements is at the expense of the faculty. Minimum of two-years of acute care medical surgical nursing practice within the last five years (or) recent medical surgical clinical teaching experience. Candidates must be able to teach in the classroom, lab, and clinical settings as assigned. Additional Information: Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, should notify the office of Institutional Equity. To request an accommodation, report a complaint, or ask questions regarding WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy (#0.2040), please contact Ms. Ena Demir, Executive Director/Title IX Coordinator via email at ena.demir@wku.edu or by phone at (270) 745-6867. Ms. Demir is also responsible for coordinating the University's response to complaints related to sex and gender harassment. Additional information regarding Title IX is accessible via WKU's https://www.wku.edu/titleix/ website. Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: http://www.wku.edu/atwku/academics.php For information related to job postings, please email employment@wku.edu . Part-time Attendant, Control Desk Department: Campus Recreation & Wellness Posted On: Apr, 27th 2026 Location: Bowling Green, KY Category: Staff Show Job Details for Part-time Attendant, Control Desk Apply Now for Part-time Attendant, Control Desk Control Desk Attendants are the first point of contact for Campus Recreation & Wellness. This position focuses on customer service, front-desk operations, and supporting a welcoming and safe facility environment. Attendants work alongside student supervisors and professional staff and play an important role in daily facility operations. This position is ideal for those looking for a job with flexible scheduling, consistent hours, and opportunities for growth. Primary Duties and Responsibilities: Greet patrons and provide friendly, professional customer service Monitor the control desk area and support operations at the main entrance. Manage towel service and equipment checkout/return Answer phone calls and respond to general questions about facilities, programs, and services Maintain a clean and organized desk area and complete light housekeeping duties Support building emergency action procedures (EAP) as directed by supervisors Job Requirements: 16 years of age or older American Red Cross CPR/AED (Adult, Child, Infant) and First Aid Certification or willingness to get certified by department upon hire Additional Information: Hourly Rate:  $9.00 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, should notify the office of Institutional Equity. To request an accommodation, report a complaint, or ask questions regarding WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy (#0.2040), please contact Ms. Ena Demir, Executive Director/Title IX Coordinator via email at ena.demir@wku.edu or by phone at (270) 745-6867. Ms. Demir is also responsible for coordinating the University's response to complaints related to sex and gender harassment. Additional information regarding Title IX is accessible via WKU's https://www.wku.edu/titleix/ website. Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: http://www.wku.edu/atwku/academics.php For information related to job postings, please email employment@wku.edu . First Previous 5 (current) 6 7 8 9 Next Last Some of the links on this page may require additional software to view. Downloads Download Acrobat Reader Download Quicktime Western Kentucky University 1906 College Heights Blvd. Bowling Green, KY 42101 Search WKU About WKU Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Transparency & Accountability Accessibility Title IX Careers Statement of Non-Discrimination Contact Us Site Index Privacy Statement Last Modified 9/17/25"
